trix $R$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403328 :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 1$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nF = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nG = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nH = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $F$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $H$ has $1$ row and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $G$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476006 :question/problem "Which of the following is a $1\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nP = \\begin{bmatrix}-0.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nQ = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nR = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $P$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $1$ row and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 3.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476021 :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nP = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -3 & -0.1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1.1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nQ = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & -0.1 \\\\ -0.1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nR = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & \\sqrt{3} & -0.1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $P$ has 